# The construction loop on the basic content set, from a fresh game, with no install: a person places a sawmill site and a woodcutter's site,
# a digger levels the sawmill's ground, the castle's planks and stones reach both sites over the roads and the builders build them, the
# woodcutter's logs reach the sawmill, and the planks it saws build a third site, a stonecutter's, that the castle could not pay for.
# It needs no install and no SIEDLER_DIR. Run it with seed 1234567812345634 and size 1 (picked with `mise run seed-info -- --content-set
# basic --seed 1234567812345634`):
#   sh tools/play-run.sh basic-construction --game-view --content-set basic --seed 1234567812345634 --size 1 --fps 10
# On that map the castle stands at 24,3, so its flag is at 25,4. The castle holds 6 planks and 5 stones at the start: the sawmill
# (3 planks, 2 stones) and the woodcutter's hut (2 planks) take 5 planks and 2 stones, so one plank and 3 stones stay, and the stonecutter's
# hut (2 planks) waits for the sawmill's planks. The sawmill's site at 25,1 has its flag at 26,2, the woodcutter's at 26,4 its flag at 27,5. The rules are the basic
# set's stand-ins (ADR 0018), so the values differ from the History Edition's `play/full-loop.play`.
expect seed = 1234567812345634
expect size = 1
wait 0.3
click-tile 24 3
wait 0.3
expect planks = 6
expect stones = 5
dump castle
shot castle 24 3 3 2

# The sawmill's site, a large building on a site for one, and the woodcutter's: each brings its flag south-east of it.
button Sawmill
click-tile 25 1
button Sawmill
button Woodcutter
click-tile 26 4
button Woodcutter
wait 0.3
expect-at 25 1 sawmill
expect-at 26 4 woodcutter-hut
expect-at 26 2 flag
expect-at 27 5 flag

# The roads to the castle's flag at 25,4: three steps north, east, and north to the sawmill's flag, and two steps south-east and east to
# the woodcutter's.
button Road
click-tile 25 4
click-tile 25 3
click-tile 26 3
click-tile 26 2
button Road
button Road
click-tile 25 4
click-tile 26 5
click-tile 27 5
button Road
wait 0.3
expect-count road = 6
shot sites 25 3 4 2
list sites

# The castle hands 5 of its planks and 2 of its stones out to the two sites' flags, and its carriers take them over the roads.
fast-forward until planks = 1 max 20000
wait 0.3
expect planks = 1
expect stones = 3
dump handed-out
shot handed-out 25 3 4 2

# The castle holds one plank now. A third site, a stonecutter's at 23,4 with its flag at 24,5, can be paid for only by the planks the sawmill
# saws from the woodcutter's logs.
button Stonecutter
click-tile 23 4
button Stonecutter
wait 0.3
expect-at 24 5 flag
button Road
wait 0.3
click-tile 25 4
wait 0.3
click-tile 25 5
wait 0.3
click-tile 24 5
wait 0.3
button Road
wait 0.3
expect-at 23 4 stonecutter-hut
expect-count road = 8
expect planks = 1

# The sawmill is built, and its sawmiller walks in and waits for a log.
fast-forward until count saws >= 1 max 60000
wait 0.3
name mill 25 1 sawmill
expect mill.constructing = false
dump sawmill-built
shot sawmill-built 25 1 3 2

# The stonecutter's site is built from the planks of the sawmill: its worker walks in and looks for a heap.
fast-forward until count looks-for-heap >= 1 max 300000
wait 0.3
name hut 23 4 stonecutter-hut
expect hut.constructing = false
name woodcutter-hut 26 4 woodcutter-hut
expect woodcutter-hut.constructing = false
dump full-loop
shot full-loop 25 3 5 2
list full-loop

# The castle held 11 logs at the start and the sawmill saws them first. When the castle's logs are gone, the planks that go on arriving at the
# castle are sawn from the logs the woodcutter fells: they travel from his flag to the sawmill's, and the planks back to the castle.
fast-forward until logs = 0 max 300000
shot logs-gone 25 3 5 2
dump logs-gone
expect logs = 0
expect planks >= 1
fast-forward until planks >= 30 max 300000
wait 0.3
expect logs = 0
expect planks >= 30
shot more-planks 25 3 5 2
dump more-planks
